      "q": "4. Long Answer Questions.\nQ1. Describe the key features of an empire and explain why empires were often fragile despite their size and power.",
      "a": "wer:\nKey features of an empire include a strong central authority, large army, administration with officials, collection of tribute or taxes, control over resources, and encouragement of trade and culture. However, empires were often fragile because they united diverse people using force, and could quickly break apart if the emperor was weak, resources declined, or groups sought independence.\nEmpires required efficient administration and military strength.\nDiversity posed challenges of unity and control.\nWeak rulers, invasions, or economic crises often led to decline.\nQ2. Analyze how Kautilya\u2019s ideas in the Arthashastra shaped the governance of the Mauryan Empire. Give examples.\nAnswer:\nKautilya\u2019s Arthashastra emphasized strong central control, detailed administration, and welfare of people. His 'Saptanga' theory defined seven elements of a state. The Mauryan Empire had organized officials, fortified cities, and infrastructure. Ashoka\u2019s welfare policies were also influenced by Kautilya\u2019s focus on harmony and duty towards citizens.\nCentralized authority, efficient taxation, and intelligence network.\nWelfare works and public infrastructure.\nEncouragement of agriculture and trade for prosperity."
