      "q": "3.  Short Answer Questions.\nQ1. Why is the Gupta period often called the \u2018classical age\u2019 of India?",
      "a": "wer:\nThe Gupta period is called the \u2018classical age\u2019 because of major developments in art, architecture, literature, science, and mathematics. The stability and prosperity of the empire allowed creativity and learning to flourish, producing works and ideas that are admired even today.\nQ2. How did land grants support the administration during Gupta times?\nAnswer:\nThe Gupta rulers granted land to local chieftains, priests, and officials. These grants, often recorded on copper plates, helped decentralize power, ensured loyalty, and generated revenue through taxes used for administration, the army, temples, and supporting scholars and the arts.\nQ3. Who was Prabh\u0101vat\u012b Gupta and what role did she play in the empire?\nAnswer:\nPrabh\u0101vat\u012b Gupta was the daughter of Chandragupta II. She ruled as a regent in the V\u0101k\u0101\u1e6daka kingdom after her husband\u2019s death, strengthening ties between the Guptas and V\u0101k\u0101\u1e6dakas and contributing to temple construction and administration.\nQ4. Explain one key achievement of \u0100ryabha\u1e6da during the Gupta period.\nAnswer:\n\u0100ryabha\u1e6da accurately calculated planetary motions and explained that the Earth spins on its axis. He also estimated the length of the year and explained eclipses, laying the foundations for Indian mathematics and astronomy."
