      "q": "2. Very Short Answer (VSA).\nQ1. Define the term 't\u012brtha'.",
      "a": "wer:\n'T\u012brtha' literally means a crossing place and symbolically refers to a sacred site where people move from ordinary life to a higher spiritual state.\nQ2. What is a sacred grove?\nAnswer:\nA sacred grove is a patch of forest protected for religious reasons and considered an abode of a local deity, often preserving unique biodiversity.\nQ3. Name any two rivers considered sacred in India.\nAnswer:\nGanga and Yamuna are both considered sacred rivers in India and are worshipped in various rituals and pilgrimages.\nQ4. Mention one purpose of pilgrimage in Indian traditions.\nAnswer:\nOne purpose of pilgrimage is to seek spiritual upliftment by visiting sacred places associated with religious or legendary events."
